### End-to-end authenticated API smoke test (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### 1. Register a user (auto-creates a default Monday semester and returns JWT tokens)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Adi",
  "email": "adi@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
    client.global.set("semesterId", response.body.activeSemesterId);
%}

### 2. Fetch & update my profile
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Adi Popescu",
  "hasCompletedOnboarding": true,
  "defaultReminderOffsetsCsv": "15,60"
}

### 3. Refresh access token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}" }

### 4. Forgot password (dev mode logs 6-digit code if MAIL_HOST is blank)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "adi@example.com" }

### 5. Create a subject with its required activities
POST http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/{{semesterId}}/subjects
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mobile Systems and Applications",
  "colorHex": "#0288D1",
  "requirements": [
    { "activityType": "LECTURE" },
    { "activityType": "LABORATORY" },
    { "activityType": "CUSTOM", "customTypeName": "Project" }
  ]
}

> {%
    client.global.set("subjectId", response.body.id);
    client.global.set("lectureReqId", response.body.requirements[0].id);
    client.global.set("labReqId", response.body.requirements[1].id);
    client.global.set("projectReqId", response.body.requirements[2].id);
%}

### 6. Unscheduled activities (the banner)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/{{semesterId}}/requirements/unscheduled
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 7. Schedule the lecture: Monday 08-10, weeks 1-10, with notes & reminders
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requirements/{{lectureReqId}}/timetable-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dayOfWeek": 1,
  "startTime": "08:00",
  "endTime": "10:00",
  "weekFrom": 1,
  "weekTo": 10,
  "room": "A101",
  "teacher": "Prof. Turing",
  "notes": "Bring laptop for live demo",
  "notificationsEnabled": true,
  "reminderOffsetsCsv": "15,60"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("lectureEntryId", response.body.id);
%}

### 8. Mark the lecture as "Canceled this week only" (ISO year-week 202648)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/timetable-entries/{{lectureEntryId}}/cancellations/202648
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 9. Restore the lecture for week 202648
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/timetable-entries/{{lectureEntryId}}/cancellations/202648
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 10. Laboratory on odd weeks, Monday 10-12
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requirements/{{labReqId}}/timetable-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dayOfWeek": 1, "startTime": "10:00", "endTime": "12:00", "weekParity": "ODD", "room": "Lab 302" }

### 11. Overlaps the lecture in weeks 1-10 -> 409 with "conflicts"
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requirements/{{projectReqId}}/timetable-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dayOfWeek": 1, "startTime": "09:00", "endTime": "11:00" }

### 12. Same request, forced
POST http://localhost:8080/api/requirements/{{projectReqId}}/timetable-entries?force=true
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "dayOfWeek": 1, "startTime": "09:00", "endTime": "11:00" }

### 13. What happens in week 2 (odd lab is hidden)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/{{semesterId}}/timetable?week=2
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 14. Create an Exam / Academic Event linked to the subject
POST http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/{{semesterId}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subjectId": {{subjectId}},
  "title": "Mobile Systems Midterm",
  "eventType": "MIDTERM",
  "eventDate": "2026-11-18",
  "startTime": "10:00",
  "endTime": "12:00",
  "room": "Aula A1",
  "notes": "Chapters 1-5",
  "notificationsEnabled": true,
  "reminderOffsetsCsv": "15,60,1440"
}

### 15. List Academic Events for the semester
GET http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/{{semesterId}}/events
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 16. Grades and averages
POST http://localhost:8080/api/subjects/{{subjectId}}/grades
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "score": 9.5, "weight": 1 }

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/subjects/{{subjectId}}/grades
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "score": 10, "weight": 1.5 }

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/subjects/{{subjectId}}/grades/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET http://localhost:8080/api/semesters/{{semesterId}}/gpa
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
